From 0b5e7fa0c5ce94a57c11711c0b8ccc4c7b5b8447 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HighAsCG (WO-870)
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 17:15:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(planner): space estimate measures what the exclude list
 really leaves out

CheckDiskSpace estimates the squashfs input as statfs("/") used space minus
estimateExcludedKiB(). That estimate skipped every exclude line containing
'*' or '!', and for a directory on the root filesystem it added only the
sizes of its directory entries (a few KiB), so a large excluded tree such as
home/*/media/* was still counted in full. On a host where that tree dominates
the root filesystem the pre-check fails with "Not enough space" although the
real ISO is small; for an excluded mount point it subtracted that other
filesystem's used space, which is not part of the root figure at all.

The excluded size is now measured: the exclude list is parsed and matched
the way mksquashfs -wildcards -ef does (process_exclude_file/add_path/
excluded_match in squashfs-tools 4.7: '/'-separated components, each matched
with fnmatch(FNM_PATHNAME|FNM_PERIOD|FNM_EXTMATCH), including the extglob
groups the built-in list uses such as boot/grub/!(themes|unicode.pf2)), and
the root filesystem is walked along the patterns only. Every excluded entry
adds st_blocks of itself and its subtree. Symlinks are not followed, other
filesystems are not entered, hard links count once and an excluded entry is
not descended again, so nested excludes are not counted twice. "... "
(non-anchored) lines are left out of the sum, which only keeps the estimate
on the safe side. The report shows how long the scan took.

The matcher was checked against glibc 2.43 fnmatch(3) with the same flags on
244,480 pattern/name pairs (curated corpus plus random fuzz): no difference.

Built and measured for HighAsCG WO-870 (730 GiB media tree excluded on the
root filesystem): estimate 247.8 GiB -> 11.9 GiB (xz); scan 0.87 s.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
